[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4525051292","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119683#issuecomment-4525051292","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119683","id":4525051292,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDbbNnA","user":{"login":"CreatedBySeb","id":11736217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzM2MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11736217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb","html_url":"https://github.com/CreatedBySeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-23T10:24:39Z","updated_at":"2026-05-23T10:24:39Z","body":"This is a question rather than a bug, it may be a better fit for the Godot contributors chat: https://chat.godotengine.org\n\nIf you feel this is a bug or is a clear enhancement, maybe provide a clear explanation of why you need it to not be const.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4525051292/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4526497749","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119683#issuecomment-4526497749","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119683","id":4526497749,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDczf1Q","user":{"login":"sockeye-d","id":106356149,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlbdtQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106356149?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d","html_url":"https://github.com/sockeye-d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-23T20:52:00Z","updated_at":"2026-05-23T20:52:00Z","body":"I think it's at least also a bug, given that the internal syntax highlighting implementations don't adhere to its const-ness.\n\nI have a SyntaxHighlighter implementation based on a tree-sitter query, and I only want to parse and re-run the query when the text of the text edit actually changes. To do this I track the hash of the last parsed string and compare it to the current text's hash, and only when they differ do I rebuild the syntax highlighting cache, since _update_cache seems to get called whenever Godot feels like it. To work around this, I just have\n\n```cpp\ngodot::Dictionary _get_line_syntax_highlighting_impl(int32_t p_line);\n```\nand \n```cpp\ngodot::Dictionary _get_line_syntax_highlighting(const int32_t p_line) const override {\n\treturn const_cast<TreeSitterSyntaxHighlighter*>(this)->_get_line_syntax_highlighting_impl(p_line);\n}\n```\n\nwhich I would really rather not do, since I think it's UB to mutate a `const_cast`ed pointer.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4526497749/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4534473324","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119683#issuecomment-4534473324","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119683","id":4534473324,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDkaSbA","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-25T13:02:15Z","updated_at":"2026-05-25T13:02:15Z","body":"To avoid `const_cast` you could declare your class state as `mutable`?\n\nIf we did want to change the `const`-ness of this virtual method, though, it is possible to do without breaking compat u